# Both images build from the repo root, so this is the ONLY dockerignore that
# takes effect. `client/.dockerignore` and `server/.dockerignore` used to sit
# here doing nothing: BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` and then
# `<context>/.dockerignore`, and with `context: .` neither of those was them.
#
# `**/node_modules` is the load-bearing line. The Dockerfiles `COPY server ./server`
# AFTER `npm ci`, so a host node_modules directory would land on top of the
# workspace tree the image just installed - host-built binaries and, worse, a
# nested `server/node_modules` shadowing the hoisted root one.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.vite

.git
.gitignore
.env
**/.env
**/.npm
**/.cache
**/npm-debug.log

client/playwright-report
client/test-results
.dev
.superpowers
